+# Patch 0054: B7c Docs Worker
+
+Attribution: Copilot-authored; review pending.
+
+## What changed
+- [x] Added `docs-server/`, a read-only Cloudflare Worker for the generated help bundle.
+- [x] Added a searchable responsive help site with cumulative Basic/Deep/Advanced levels and Mermaid diagrams.
+- [x] Added `/api/index` and `/api/page/:id`, version ETags, and `304 Not Modified`.
+- [x] Added optional app-side refresh through `EXPO_PUBLIC_DOCS_URL`; keep built-in pages on no URL, unchanged content or request failure.
+- [x] Added setup and deployment notes. Custom domain and storefront styling remain in E1.
+- [x] Validation: `npm --prefix docs-server run typecheck`, app `npm run typecheck`, focused help tests, and local Worker/API/browser smoke tests.
+
+## Review
+- [ ] User: configure `EXPO_PUBLIC_DOCS_URL` after deploying the Worker if online Help updates are wanted.
+- [ ] User: deploy and verify the Worker on your Cloudflare account.
diff --git a/docs-server/README.md b/docs-server/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..27e8db7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs-server/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# POS documentation Worker
+
+This Cloudflare Worker serves the same generated help bundle that ships inside the iPad app. It has no database, secrets or user data.
+
+## Develop and deploy
+
+```sh
+cd docs-server
+npm install
+npx wrangler login
+npm run dev
+npm run deploy
+```
+
+`npm run deploy` rebuilds `../help/help.json` first. The Worker prints its `workers.dev` URL after deployment. Custom-domain styling and a dedicated subdomain are tracked separately under E1.
+
+To let the app check for newer help at startup, set `EXPO_PUBLIC_DOCS_URL` to the deployed Worker origin when building the app. Without it, the app always uses its built-in, offline copy.
+
+## Routes
+
+- `GET /` serves the searchable help site with Basic, Deep and Advanced levels, page navigation, and full Mermaid diagrams.
+- `GET /api/index` returns the versioned help bundle. The version is also the HTTP `ETag`; send `If-None-Match` to receive `304 Not Modified`.
+- `GET /api/page/<id>` returns one page and the bundle version, also with the version `ETag`.
+
+The browser-rendered site sanitises Markdown HTML and runs Mermaid in strict security mode. API responses are read-only and contain only published help text.
